@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — A role audience follows role changes
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
actor "Role grantor (AssignRoles)" as admin
actor "Member holding role R" as m
participant "RolesHandler" as roles
participant "ResourcesEndpoints" as ep
participant "ListResourcesHandler" as h
participant "ResourceAccess" as acc
database "Community database" as db
note over db: "Team kit" is Shared with role definition R
m -> ep : GET /api/resources
ep -> h : ListAsync(...)
h -> acc : Visible(Resources, caller held roles = {R})
acc -> db : ... OR EXISTS ResourceShareRole WHERE RoleDefinitionId IN (R)
db --> m : "Team kit" listed
admin -> roles : Remove role R from the member (L2-138)
roles -> db : Profile roles updated (no resource changes)
m -> ep : GET /api/resources/{kit id}
ep -> acc : VisibleOrOwnArchived(caller held roles = {})
acc -> db : No matching share row
ep --> m : 404 (L2-060 AC8)
admin -> roles : Grant role R to another member
note right of roles
  The new holder of R can open the kit on their next request
  and gets no ResourceShared notification (L2-061 AC3)
end note
@enduml
